Hi @participant1, this patch has worked for us, all tests passing on x86_64 and ppc64le. If you confirm its correct, we can raise a PR:
```
diff --git a/community/io/src/main/java/org/neo4j/io/pagecache/impl/muninn/PageList.java b/community/io/src/main/java/org/neo4j/io/pagecache/impl/muninn/PageList.java
index 2b6bec387fa..777af76842e 100644
--- a/community/io/src/main/java/org/neo4j/io/pagecache/impl/muninn/PageList.java
+++ b/community/io/src/main/java/org/neo4j/io/pagecache/impl/muninn/PageList.java
@@ -273,7 +273,11 @@ class PageList implements PageReferenceTranslator {
     long initBuffer(long pageRef) {
         var address = getAddress(pageRef);
         if (address == 0L) {
-            address = memoryAllocator.allocateAligned(getCachePageSize(), bufferAlignment);
+            if (bufferAlignment == UnsafeUtil.pageSize()) {
+                address = memoryAllocator.allocateAligned(getCachePageSize(), getCachePageSize());
+            } else {
+                address = memoryAllocator.allocateAligned(getCachePageSize(), bufferAlignment);
+            }
             UnsafeUtil.putLong(offAddress(pageRef), address);
         }
         return address;

```
cc: @participant4

@reporter This issue is already patched and will be part of the Neo4j 5.9 release next month. The patch will cap the alignment to 8K, basically 

```
address = memoryAllocator.allocateAligned(getCachePageSize(), Math.min(getCachePageSize(), bufferAlignment));
```

This is not enough to support larger page sizes completely though. There are some other issues regarding page size >8K that are also addressed by the same patch.

Fortunately for you, ARM also supports 64K TLB entries :)
